THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS ARE NOT COVERED BY THIS NOTICE.
  vendor/three.module.js is Three.js (https://threejs.org), Copyright 2010-2024
Three.js Authors, licensed under the MIT licence, vendored here unmodified
except for the build packaged by the maintainers. It keeps its own licence and
may be used under that licence's terms.

  assets/earth-blue-marble-1280.jpg is a NASA Blue Marble / MODIS-derived
public-domain image. Source record: NASA Visible Earth image 57730 / Blue Marble
collection, with the local 1280px derivative downloaded from Wikimedia Commons
file "Land shallow topo 2048.jpg" (NASA credit: Reto Stöckli / NASA GSFC,
Robert Simmon and MODIS/USGS support teams). The NASA-derived map is included as
an external public-domain asset and is not claimed by this proprietary notice.

  assets/moon-lroc-color-2048.jpg and assets/moon-ldem-1024.jpg are NASA lunar
maps from the Scientific Visualization Studio's "CGI Moon Kit"
(https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/4720/): the LROC WAC colour mosaic, assembled by the
LRO Camera team, and the LDEM elevation map from LRO's laser altimeter (LOLA).
Credit: NASA's Scientific Visualization Studio — Ernie Wright, Noah Petro (USRA).
Public domain. The local files are resized derivatives of the kit's own maps, and
are likewise not claimed by this proprietary notice.

  The night-side city-light layer on the Earth is GENERATED by this project from
the land and ocean colours of the bundled Blue Marble map (see buildNightLights in
src/three/SolarSystem.js). It is a visual model, not a city-lights dataset, and
must not be described as measured or observed lighting.

Any other third-party dependency named in docs/ or package manifests keeps its
own licence too.

